      "role": "user",
      "content": "{\"phase\": \"synthesis\", \"official_statement_as_data\": \"Problem E\\nYet More Primes\\nPrime test is a common task in many applications, specially for security, cryptography,\\nand other interest areas. There are a number of techniques used to verify if a number is\\nprime, and the common problem is that all techniques consumes lots of time.\\nThe problem is easy to solve, giving the number to be tested and time enough to calculate.\\nBut a weird scientist took our numbers, and cut them in two halves, so we have ﬁrst to\\nre-arrange the numbers, looking for the primes. In this case, we have the certainty that all\\nthe numbers we have are primes, but the problem is how to re-order them\\nInput\\nIn the ﬁrst line, there is the numberP of prime numbers (1≤ P≤ 1000). Then, 2P lines\\nwith parts of the numbers to be tested, with no order. Prime numbers in this problem are\\ntaken as strings, so ﬁrst half and second half simply means an arbitrary cut of such string.\\nFor instance, prime number 504155039 can be cut in 5041 and 55039, or 504155 and 039\\nNote that second half numbers could begin with a lead zero, so you must take it into\\naccount. Of course, this doesn’t happen with the ﬁrst half.\\nThe input must be read from the standard input.\\nOutput\\nYou have to print the list of the P prime numbers, in ascendant order.\\nThe output must be written to the standard output.\\nExample\\nInput Output\\n4 1000213\\n50415 5041501\\n100 5575001\\n5041 504155039\\n55750 504155713\\n5039\\n01\\n0213\\n55713\\n\\n\\nThis experiment uses a reviewed finite certified input/output contract only. There are six private research cases and six distinct private confirmation cases. P is in {1,2,4,8,16,30}; the input lists two separately permuted groups of P decimal fragments. Left fragments have no leading zero and end in an even digit; right fragments have seven characters including a leading zero. Each original pair comes from a true prime and the multiset of every admissible prime concatenation equals the P source occurrences. Concatenations are at most 600971707; output is compared as exact bytes. The official example has an unresolved P/output-count contradiction. No claim is made for the whole contest domain or arbitrary fragment orders. The fixed benchmark is one member of the same certified finite set; no hidden values or expected outputs are supplied. Target: Linux ARM64, four CPU cores, 16 GiB RAM, zero GPUs. Compilation: GCC -O2 -std=c11 -Werror=uninitialized -Werror=maybe-uninitialized -lm.\", \"current_sources_as_data\": {\"src/model-view/primetest.c\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\r\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\r\\n#include <math.h>\\r\\n#include <string.h>\\r\\n\\r\\n#define MAXNUM 100\\r\\n#define MAXSTR 50\\r\\n#define MAXRESULTS 1000\\r\\n\\r\\nchar firstHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\\r\\nchar secondHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\\r\\nchar strToTest[MAXSTR];\\r\\nlong int result[MAXRESULTS];\\r\\nint numPrimes=0;\\r\\n\\r\\nint isprime(long int value)\\r\\n{ long int root;\\r\\n  long int factor=2;\\r\\n  int prime=1;\\r\\n  root = sqrtl(value);\\r\\n  while ((factor<=root) && (prime))\\r\\n        { prime = fmod((double)value,(double) factor) > 0.0;\\r\\n\\t\\t  factor++;\\r\\n\\t    }\\r\\n  return prime;\\r\\n}\\r\\n\\r\\nvoid quicksort(long int *primes,int first,int last)\\r\\n{ int i, j, pivot;\\r\\n  long int temp;\\r\\n\\r\\n  if (first<last)\\r\\n     { pivot=first;\\r\\n       i=first;\\r\\n       j=last;\\r\\n       while(i<j)\\r\\n\\t     { while (primes[i]<=primes[pivot]&&i<last)\\r\\n             i++;\\r\\n           while(primes[j]>primes[pivot])\\r\\n             j--;\\r\\n           if (i<j)\\r\\n\\t\\t      { temp=primes[i];\\r\\n                primes[i]=primes[j];\\r\\n                primes[j]=temp;\\r\\n              }\\r\\n         }\\r\\n       temp=primes[pivot];\\r\\n       primes[pivot]=primes[j];\\r\\n       primes[j]=temp;\\r\\n       quicksort(primes,first,j-1);\\r\\n       quicksort(primes,j+1,last);\\r\\n     }\\r\\n}\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nint main(int argc,char** argv)\\r\\n{ FILE *primesFile;\\r\\n  int i=0,j=0,numResults=0;\\r\\n  long int primeToTest;\\r\\n  primesFile=stdin;\\r\\n  fscanf(primesFile,\\\"%d\\\\n\\\",&numPrimes);\\r\\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\\r\\n      fscanf(primesFile,\\\"%s\\\\n\\\",firstHalf[i]);\\r\\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\\r\\n      fscanf(primesFile,\\\"%s\\\\n\\\",secondHalf[i]);\\r\\n  fclose(primesFile);\\r\\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\\r\\n\\t  for (j=0;j<numPrimes;j++)\\r\\n\\t      { strcpy(strToTest,firstHalf[i]);\\r\\n\\t        strcat(strToTest,secondHalf[j]);\\r\\n\\t\\t\\tprimeToTest=atol(strToTest);\\r\\n\\t\\t\\tif (isprime(primeToTest)) \\r\\n\\t\\t\\t   { result[numResults++]=primeToTest;\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t   }\\r\\n\\t      }\\r\\n  quicksort(result,0,numResults-1);\\r\\n  for (i=0;i<numResults;i++)\\r\\n      printf(\\\"%ld\\\\n\\\",result[i]);\\t  \\r\\n  return 0;\\r\\n}\", \"src/sources/primetest.c\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\r\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\r\\n#include <math.h>\\r\\n#include <string.h>\\r\\n\\r\\n#define MAXNUM 100\\r\\n#define MAXSTR 50\\r\\n#define MAXRESULTS 1000\\r\\n\\r\\nchar firstHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\\r\\nchar secondHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\\r\\nchar strToTest[MAXSTR];\\r\\nlong int result[MAXRESULTS];\\r\\nint numPrimes=0;\\r\\n\\r\\nint isprime(long int value)\\r\\n{ long int root;\\r\\n  long int factor=2;\\r\\n  int prime=1;\\r\\n  root = sqrtl(value);\\r\\n  while ((factor<=root) && (prime))\\r\\n        { prime = fmod((double)value,(double) factor) > 0.0;\\r\\n\\t\\t  factor++;\\r\\n\\t    }\\r\\n  return prime;\\r\\n}\\r\\n\\r\\nvoid quicksort(long int *primes,int first,int last)\\r\\n{ int i, j, pivot;\\r\\n  long int temp;\\r\\n\\r\\n  if (first<last)\\r\\n     { pivot=first;\\r\\n       i=first;\\r\\n       j=last;\\r\\n       while(i<j)\\r\\n\\t     { while (primes[i]<=primes[pivot]&&i<last)\\r\\n             i++;\\r\\n           while(primes[j]>primes[pivot])\\r\\n             j--;\\r\\n           if (i<j)\\r\\n\\t\\t      { temp=primes[i];\\r\\n                primes[i]=primes[j];\\r\\n                primes[j]=temp;\\r\\n              }\\r\\n         }\\r\\n       temp=primes[pivot];\\r\\n       primes[pivot]=primes[j];\\r\\n       primes[j]=temp;\\r\\n       quicksort(primes,first,j-1);\\r\\n       quicksort(primes,j+1,last);\\r\\n     }\\r\\n}\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nint main(int argc,char** argv)\\r\\n{ FILE *primesFile;\\r\\n  int i=0,j=0,numResults=0;\\r\\n  long int primeToTest;\\r\\n  primesFile=stdin;\\r\\n  fscanf(primesFile,\\\"%d\\\\n\\\",&numPrimes);\\r\\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\\r\\n      fscanf(primesFile,\\\"%s\\\\n\\\",firstHalf[i]);\\r\\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\\r\\n      fscanf(primesFile,\\\"%s\\\\n\\\",secondHalf[i]);\\r\\n  fclose(primesFile);\\r\\n  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\\r\\n\\t  for (j=0;j<numPrimes;j++)\\r\\n\\t      { strcpy(strToTest,firstHalf[i]);\\r\\n\\t        strcat(strToTest,secondHalf[j]);\\r\\n\\t\\t\\tprimeToTest=atol(strToTest);\\r\\n\\t\\t\\tif (isprime(primeToTest)) \\r\\n\\t\\t\\t   { result[numResults++]=primeToTest;\\r\\n\\t\\t\\t   }\\r\\n\\t      }\\r\\n  quicksort(result,0,numResults-1);\\r\\n  for (i=0;i<numResults;i++)\\r\\n      printf(\\\"%ld\\\\n\\\",result[i]);\\t  \\r\\n  return 0;\\r\\n}\"}, \"automatic_observations_as_data\": {\"sources\": [{\"id\": \"6a8571a740854bf6\", \"role\": \"A\", \"commit\": \"c1a46c381c12b854b60964bc7c1e70d1a6136330\", \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/model-view/primetest.c\", \"src/sources/primetest.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Parse fragments into numeric values while retaining each right fragment's decimal scale, then materialize all pair concatenations contiguously in row-major order.\", \"Build one dense byte sieve through the integer square root of the maximum candidate and classify candidates using its ascending prime list, stopping when factor > value/factor.\", \"Compact primes in place without deduplicating, then sort and print the result values.\"]}, \"mean_seconds\": 0.005129319615662098, \"diff\": \"diff --git a/src/model-view/primetest.c b/src/model-view/primetest.c\\nindex fbc86e2..995b39a 100644\\n--- a/src/model-view/primetest.c\\n+++ b/src/model-view/primetest.c\\n@@ -1,80 +1,239 @@\\n-#include <stdio.h>\\n-#include <stdlib.h>\\n-#include <math.h>\\n-#include <string.h>\\n-\\n-#define MAXNUM 100\\n-#define MAXSTR 50\\n-#define MAXRESULTS 1000\\n-\\n-char firstHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\\n-char secondHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\\n-char strToTest[MAXSTR];\\n-long int result[MAXRESULTS];\\n-int numPrimes=0;\\n-\\n-int isprime(long int value)\\n-{ long int root;\\n-  long int factor=2;\\n-  int prime=1;\\n-  root = sqrtl(value);\\n-  while ((factor<=root) && (prime))\\n-        { prime = fmod((double)value,(double) factor) > 0.0;\\n-\\t\\t  factor++;\\n-\\t    }\\n-  return prime;\\n-}\\n-\\n-void quicksort(long int *primes,int first,int last)\\n-{ int i, j, pivot;\\n-  long int temp;\\n-\\n-  if (first<last)\\n-     { pivot=first;\\n-       i=first;\\n-       j=last;\\n-       while(i<j)\\n-\\t     { while (primes[i]<=primes[pivot]&&i<last)\\n-             i++;\\n-           while(primes[j]>primes[pivot])\\n-             j--;\\n-           if (i<j)\\n-\\t\\t      { temp=primes[i];\\n-                primes[i]=primes[j];\\n-                primes[j]=temp;\\n-              }\\n-         }\\n-       temp=primes[pivot];\\n-       primes[pivot]=primes[j];\\n-       primes[j]=temp;\\n-       quicksort(primes,first,j-1);\\n-       quicksort(primes,j+1,last);\\n-     }\\n-}\\n-\\n-\\n-int main(int argc,char** argv)\\n-{ FILE *primesFile;\\n-  int i=0,j=0,numResults=0;\\n-  long int primeToTest;\\n-  primesFile=stdin;\\n-  fscanf(primesFile,\\\"%d\\\\n\\\",&numPrimes);\\n-  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\\n-      fscanf(primesFile,\\\"%s\\\\n\\\",firstHalf[i]);\\n-  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\\n-      fscanf(primesFile,\\\"%s\\\\n\\\",secondHalf[i]);\\n-  fclose(primesFile);\\n-  for (i=0;i<numPrimes;i++)\\n-\\t  for (j=0;j<numPrimes;j++)\\n-\\t      { strcpy(strToTest,firstHalf[i]);\\n-\\t        strcat(strToTest,secondHalf[j]);\\n-\\t\\t\\tprimeToTest=atol(strToTest);\\n-\\t\\t\\tif (isprime(primeToTest)) \\n-\\t\\t\\t   { result[numResults++]=primeToTest;\\n-\\t\\t\\t   }\\n-\\t      }\\n-  quicksort(result,0,numResults-1);\\n-  for (i=0;i<numResults;i++)\\n-      printf(\\\"%ld\\\\n\\\",result[i]);\\t  \\n-  return 0;\\n-}\\n\\\\ No newline at end of file\\n+#include <ctype.h>\\n+#include <inttypes.h>\\n+#include <stdint.h>\\n+#include <stdio.h>\\n+#include <stdlib.h>\\n+#include <string.h>\\n+\\n+typedef struct {\\n+    uint64_t value;\\n+    uint64_t scale;\\n+} Fragment;\\n+\\n+static char *read_token(FILE *stream)\\n+{\\n+    int ch;\\n+    size_t capacity = 32;\\n+    size_t length = 0;\\n+    char *token;\\n+\\n+    do {\\n+        ch = fgetc(stream);\\n+    } while (ch != EOF && isspace((unsigned char)ch));\\n+    if (ch == EOF)\\n+        return NULL;\\n+\\n+    token = malloc(capacity);\\n+    if (token == NULL)\\n+        return NULL;\\n+\\n+    while (ch != EOF && !isspace((unsigned char)ch)) {\\n+        if (length + 1 >= capacity) {\\n+            size_t new_capacity = capacity * 2;\\n+            char *resized = realloc(token, new_capacity);\\n+            if (resized == NULL) {\\n+                free(token);\\n+                return NULL;\\n+            }\\n+            token = resized;\\n+            capacity = new_capacity;\\n+        }\\n+        token[length++] = (char)ch;\\n+        ch = fgetc(stream);\\n+    }\\n+    token[length] = '\\\\0';\\n+    return token;\\n+}\\n+\\n+static int parse_fragment(const char *text, Fragment *fragment)\\n+{\\n+    uint64_t value = 0;\\n+    uint64_t scale = 1;\\n+    const unsigned char *p = (const unsigned char *)text;\\n+\\n+    if (*p == '\\\\0')\\n+        return 0;\\n+    for (; *p != '\\\\0'; ++p) {\\n+        unsigned digit;\\n+        if (*p < '0' || *p > '9')\\n+            return 0;\\n+        digit = (unsigned)(*p - '0');\\n+        if (value > (UINT64_MAX - digit) / 10 || scale > UINT64_MAX / 10)\\n+            return 0;\\n+        value = value * 10 + digit;\\n+        scale *= 10;\\n+    }\\n+    fragment->value = value;\\n+    fragment->scale = scale;\\n+    return 1;\\n+}\\n+\\n+static uint64_t integer_sqrt(uint64_t value)\\n+{\\n+    uint64_t low = 0;\\n+    uint64_t high = UINT32_MAX;\\n+\\n+    while (low < high) {\\n+        uint64_t middle = low + (high - low + 1) / 2;\\n+        if (middle <= value / middle)\\n+            low = middle;\\n+        else\\n+            high = middle - 1;\\n+    }\\n+    return low;\\n+}\\n+\\n+static int is_prime_from_sieve(uint64_t value, const uint32_t *primes,\\n+                               size_t prime_count)\\n+{\\n+    size_t i;\\n+\\n+    if (value < 2)\\n+        return 0;\\n+    for (i = 0; i < prime_count; ++i) {\\n+        uint64_t factor = primes[i];\\n+        if (factor > value / factor)\\n+            break;\\n+        if (value % factor == 0)\\n+            return 0;\\n+    }\\n+    return 1;\\n+}\\n+\\n+static int compare_u64(const void *left, const void *right)\\n+{\\n+    uint64_t a = *(const uint64_t *)left;\\n+    uint64_t b = *(const uint64_t *)right;\\n+    return (a > b) - (a < b);\\n+}\\n+\\n+int main(void)\\n+{\\n+    int num_primes;\\n+    size_t count;\\n+    size_t candidate_count;\\n+    size_t i;\\n+    size_t j;\\n+    size_t result_count = 0;\\n+    uint64_t maximum = 0;\\n+    Fragment *left;\\n+    Fragment *right;\\n+    uint64_t *candidates;\\n+    uint64_t limit;\\n+    size_t sieve_size;\\n+    uint8_t *composite;\\n+    uint32_t *small_primes;\\n+    size_t prime_count = 0;\\n+    size_t prime_index = 0;\\n+\\n+    if (scanf(\\\"%d\\\", &num_primes) != 1 || num_primes < 1)\\n+        return 0;\\n+    count = (size_t)num_primes;\\n+    left = malloc(count * sizeof(*left));\\n+    right = malloc(count * sizeof(*right));\\n+    if (left == NULL || right == NULL) {\\n+        free(left);\\n+        free(right);\\n+        return 1;\\n+    }\\n+\\n+    for (i = 0; i < count; ++i) {\\n+        char *token = read_token(stdin);\\n+        int valid = token != NULL && parse_fragment(token, &left[i]);\\n+        free(token);\\n+        if (!valid) {\\n+            free(left);\\n+            free(right);\\n+            return 1;\\n+        }\\n+    }\\n+    for (i = 0; i < count; ++i) {\\n+        char *token = read_token(stdin);\\n+        int valid = token != NULL && parse_fragment(token, &right[i]);\\n+        free(token);\\n+        if (!valid) {\\n+            free(left);\\n+            free(right);\\n+            return 1;\\n+   \"}, {\"id\": \"8ab810087a9045b5\", \"role\": \"B\", \"commit\": \"60cd7897af99867d4c81556614ecfa63278f045a\", \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/model-view/primetest.c\", \"src/sources/primetest.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Added an independent candidate filter for divisors 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, and 13, using bitwise predicates so all fixed-divisor checks are available for vectorization.\", \"Handled prime candidates at or below 13 directly, then continued wheel trial division from 17 for candidates that passed the filter.\", \"Kept candidate generation and result collection semantics intact; applied ivdep only to loops whose iterations have independent memory accesses.\"]}, \"mean_seconds\": 0.0054819416254758835, \"diff\": \"diff --git a/src/model-view/primetest.c b/src/model-view/primetest.c\\nindex fbc86e2..65ff13b 100644\\n--- a/src/model-view/primetest.c\\n+++ b/src/model-view/primetest.c\\n@@ -1,80 +1,125 @@\\n-#include <stdio.h>\\n-#include <stdlib.h>\\n-#include <math.h>\\n-#include <string.h>\\n-\\n-#define MAXNUM 100\\n-#define MAXSTR 50\\n-#define MAXRESULTS 1000\\n-\\n-char firstHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\\n-char secondHalf[MAXNUM][MAXSTR];\\n-char strToTest[MAXSTR];\\n-long int result[MAXRESULTS];\\n-int numPrimes=0;\\n-\\n-int isprime(long int value)\\n-{ long int root;\\n-  long int factor=2;\\n-  int prime=1;\\n-  root = sqrtl(value);\\n-  