6c381c12b854b60964bc7c1e70d1a6136330\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.005129319615662098, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/model-view/primetest.c\", \"src/sources/primetest.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Parse fragments into numeric values while retaining each right fragment's decimal scale, then materialize all pair concatenations contiguously in row-major order.\", \"Build one dense byte sieve through the integer square root of the maximum candidate and classify candidates using its ascending prime list, stopping when factor > value/factor.\", \"Compact primes in place without deduplicating, then sort and print the result values.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"8ab810087a9045b5\", \"role\": \"B\", \"commit\": \"60cd7897af99867d4c81556614ecfa63278f045a\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.0054819416254758835, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/model-view/primetest.c\", \"src/sources/primetest.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Added an independent candidate filter for divisors 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, and 13, using bitwise predicates so all fixed-divisor checks are available for vectorization.\", \"Handled prime candidates at or below 13 directly, then continued wheel trial division from 17 for candidates that passed the filter.\", \"Kept candidate generation and result collection semantics intact; applied ivdep only to loops whose iterations have independent memory accesses.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"802481162cb645ba\", \"role\": \"B\", \"commit\": \"b220693cfd57ce5307c694636af180ac9b0f466b\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.005695889083047708, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/model-view/primetest.c\", \"src/sources/primetest.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Pre-parse both fragment groups and replace string concatenation/conversion with leftValue * 10000000 + rightValue, preserving the seven-character right-fragment width.\", \"Build the candidate matrix before classification; annotate its independent contiguous inner loop with GCC ivdep to permit vectorization without asserting away real loop-carried dependencies.\", \"Replace sqrtl/fmod trial division with exact integer checks for small factors followed by 30-wheel divisors and the overflow-safe bound factor <= value / factor.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"f8da4208a191490d\", \"role\": \"A\", \"commit\": \"1aeffd167fa68e61593bec22f5e0d9636ba78217\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.005709169432520866, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/model-view/primetest.c\", \"src/sources/primetest.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Represent each fragment as its numeric value and decimal scale, preserving the width of right-hand fragments that begin with zero.\", \"Enumerate pairs in 16-by-16 tiles with contiguous inner access to the right-fragment array, calculate candidates directly, and allocate result capacity for all P-squared pairs.\", \"Replace floating-point trial division with integer 6k±1 checks and use qsort for sorted output.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"62a89283f9684b90\", \"role\": \"C\", \"commit\": \"26399b5e34f0242beade713c4550f8d0222cfeb7\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.04373295605182648, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/model-view/primetest.c\", \"src/sources/primetest.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Use an OpenMP collapsed two-dimensional loop with dynamic scheduling and chunk size 4 when P is at least 8; retain serial processing below that granularity threshold.\", \"Move the concatenation buffer into the candidate routine and store each result in a unique matrix cell, avoiding shared mutable state and synchronization in the parallel loop.\", \"Compact the per-pair results serially and expand result capacity to cover the candidate grid.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"afa2ce5685d6406f\", \"role\": \"C\", \"commit\": \"5af41938347c35ddc6505b1e66d9d989d3ac5147\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.043739049384991326, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/model-view/primetest.c\", \"src/sources/primetest.c\"], \"retained\": [\"Extracted candidate testing into a helper with per-call string storage so iterations do not share a mutable buffer.\", \"For P >= 8, applied a collapsed, static OpenMP work-sharing loop over the independent P-squared candidate pairs; smaller inputs use a serial loop.\", \"Stored each test result in its unique candidate-index slot, then gathered and sorted the prime values serially.\", \"Sized result storage for the full MAXNUM-by-MAXNUM candidate space.\"]}}]}, \"target_as_data\": {\"architecture\": \"ARM64\", \"cpu_cores\": 4, \"gpus\": 0}, \"required_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"analysis\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"A\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"B\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"C\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"G\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"analysis\", \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"G\"]}}"
